#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "For Users with Disabilities"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the documentation discusses accessibility features in "
"&kcells; for users with disabilities. Some of these features apply to &kde; "
"as a whole and are controlled from <ulink url=\"help:kcontrol"
"\">&kcontrolcenter;</ulink>. Some apply to all &koffice; applications, and "
"some are specific to &kcells;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installing the <command>kdeaccessibility</command> Module"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "kdeaccessibility"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most of the features described in this chapter are enabled by installing the "
"<command>kdeaccessibility</command> module. The <command>kdeaccessibility</"
"command> module is part of the &kde; project <ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org"
"\">http://www.kde.org</ulink>. The <command>kdeaccessibility</command> "
"package can be obtained from &kde-ftp;, the main ftp site of the &kde; "
"project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many distributions offer precompiled binaries on their ftp sites. Please "
"check your distribution's web sites for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More information about &kde; accessibility can be obtained by visiting "
"<ulink url=\"http://accessibility.kde.org/\">http://accessibility.kde.org/</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Visual Impairments</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Visual Impairments</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kcells; is not usable by totally blind users. It is hoped that a general "
"screen reader for the blind will be available in future versions of &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Theming</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Theming</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For low-sighted or light allergic users, several features are available in "
"the &kcontrolcenter; <menuchoice><guimenu>Appearance &amp; Themes</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Theme Manager</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, like high "
"contrast color themes. If you are light allergic, the "
"<guilabel>HighContrastDark</guilabel> or <guilabel>HighContrastLight</"
"guilabel> themes may be helpful. If you have difficulty reading small fonts "
"or seeing small icons, the <guilabel>HighContrastDark-big</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>HighContrastLight-big</guilabel> themes will increase the size of "
"text, buttons, and icons. You may also customize background, colors, fonts, "
"and icons from the same dialog. A set of monochrome icons is available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose one of the <guilabel>Big</guilabel> themes, you may discover "
"that some windows are too large to fit your monitor. Purchasing a larger "
"monitor will be helpful. You can drag the portions of the window not visible "
"into the visible area by holding down the &Alt; key and dragging with the "
"&LMB; anywhere within the screen. If you have trouble operating a mouse, you "
"can also move screens by pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;"
"<keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo>. In the dropdown Windows Operations Menu, "
"choose <menuchoice><guimenuitem>Move</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Move the "
"screen with the arrow keys and press &Esc; to finish the move."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmagnifier;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "magnifier"
msgstr "lópia"

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>kdeaccessibility</command> module includes a screen magnifier "
"application called <ulink url=\"help:kmag\">&kmagnifier;</ulink>. If it is "
"installed, you can run it from <menuchoice><guimenu>K-Button</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Utilities</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>KMag (Screen "
"Magnifier)</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Text-to-Speech</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Text-to-Speech</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>TTS</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>kdeaccessibility</command> module includes a Text-to-Speech "
"component called KTTS. If KTTS is installed, you can configure &kcells; to "
"speak the text that is under the mouse pointer or speak the text of each "
"screen widget as it receives focus. Before using this feature, first "
"configure KTTS. See <ulink url=\"help:kttsd\">The KTTS Handbook</ulink> for "
"details. To turn on the TTS feature in &kcells;, select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kcells;...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. This will display a dialog box. "
"Clicking on <guilabel>TTS</guilabel> will allow you to change the following."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: a11y.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak widget under mouse pointer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, &kcells; will speak the text of each widget as the mouse "
"pointer moves over the widget."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: a11y.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak widget with focus"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, &kcells; will speak the text of each widget as it receives "
"focus."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: a11y.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak tool tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, &kcells; will speak the popup tool tip for each widget in "
"addition to the text of the widget."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: a11y.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak What's This"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, &kcells; will speak the <quote>What's This?</quote> help for "
"each widget in addition to the text of the widget."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: a11y.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "Say whether disabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, &kcells; will speak the word \"disabled\" if the widget is "
"currently disabled (grayed)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: a11y.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speak accelerators"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, &kcells; will speak the accelerator of the widget in addition "
"to the text of the widget. Accelerators are the underlined letters you see "
"in the text of the widget. For example, in the main menu, the "
"<menuchoice><guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item has the "
"\"Q\" underlined. You can choose it by pressing <keycap>Q</keycap>. To speak "
"the accelerator, check this option and enter the word you want to speak "
"before the accelerator in the <guilabel>Prefaced by the word</guilabel> box. "
"In this example shown above, &kcells; will speak \"Accelerator Q\"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: a11y.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "Polling interval"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option determines how often &kcells; will check for a change in the "
"widget under the mouse pointer or a new focused widget. You should leave "
"this option on the default setting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <guibutton>TTS</guibutton> option does not appear on this screen, you "
"do not have the KTTS component installed in your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Not all widgets are spoken. For example, the items on the main menubar are "
"not spoken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Motor Impairments and Mouseless Operation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Motor Impairments"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mouseless Operation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmousetool;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you can operate a mouse, but have trouble clicking, the <ulink url=\"help:"
"kmousetool\">&kmousetool;</ulink> application may help. Run it from "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>K-Button</guimenu><guimenuitem>Utilities</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>KMouseTool (Automatik Mouse Click)</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "XAccess Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "XAccess"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Sticky Keys</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Slow Keys</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Bounce Keys</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kcontrolcenter; offers several keyboard features collectively called "
"XAccess. They include:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: a11y.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Sticky Keys</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This feature permits operation of meta keys, such as &Alt;, &Ctrl;, and "
"&Shift; without having to hold the keys down. It is useful when you can only "
"use one finger or one hand to operate the keyboard. With Sticky Keys on, "
"press and release a &Alt;, &Ctrl;, or &Shift; key, then press another key. "
"The result is as if you pressed both keys at once. Press the &Alt;, &Ctrl;, "
"or &Shift; key again to turn off the sticky key. Activate this feature in "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>K-Button</guimenu><guimenuitem>&kcontrolcenter;</"
"guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Regional &amp; Accessibility</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Accessibility</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Modifier "
"Keys</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: a11y.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Slow Keys</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This feature is useful if you have hand tremors or difficulty accurately "
"pressing keys. It prevents inadvertent key presses by requiring that a key "
"be held down for a minimum time before it is accepted. Activate this feature "
"in <menuchoice><guimenu>K-Button</guimenu><guimenuitem>&kcontrolcenter;</"
"guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Regional &amp; Accessibility</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Accessibility</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Keyboard "
"Filters</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: a11y.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Bounce Keys</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This feature is also useful if you have hand tremors. It prevents "
"inadvertent repeated key presses by preventing another keystroke for a "
"certain amount of time. Activate this feature in <menuchoice><guimenu>K-"
"Button</guimenu><guimenuitem>&kcontrolcenter;</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Regional &amp; Accessibility</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Accessibility</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>Keyboard "
"Filters</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Mouse Emulation</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Mouse Emulation</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mouse Emulation permits you to move and click the mouse using the keyboard. "
"Press <keycombo>&Alt;<keycap>F12</keycap></keycombo> to activate it. Use the "
"arrow keys to move the mouse pointer to the desired location, and press "
"<keycap>spacebar</keycap> to \"click\" the mouse. Unfortunately, you cannot "
"use Mouse Emulation to perform &RMB; clicks or dragging."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Mouse Navigation</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: a11y.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Mouse Navigation</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This feature permits you to emulate the mouse using the numeric keypad of "
"your keyboard. To activate it, go to <menuchoice><guimenu>K-Button</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>&kcontrolcenter;</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Peripherals</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Mouse</guimenuitem> "
"<guimenuitem>Mouse Navigation</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Check the "
"<guilabel>Move pointer with keyboard (using the num pad)</guilabel> box. "
"When you do this, the other settings will become enabled, and you can "
"customize the keyboard pointer behavior further, if required. The various "
"keys on the number pad move in the direction you would expect. Note that you "
"can move diagonally as well as up, down, left and right. The <keycap>5</"
"keycap> key emulates a click to a pointer button, typically &LMB;. You "
"change which button is emulated by using the <keycap>/</keycap> key (which "
"makes it &LMB;), <keycap>*</keycap> key (which makes it middle mouse button) "
"and <keycap>-</keycap> (which makes it &RMB;). Using the <keycap>+</keycap> "
"emulates a doubleclick to the selected pointer button. You can use the "
"<keycap>0</keycap> key to emulate holding down the selected pointer button "
"(for easy dragging), and then use the <keycap>.</keycap> to emulate "
"releasing the selected pointer button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <keycap>Menu</keycap> key to pop up the context menu. On most "
"keyboards, the <keycap>Menu</keycap> key is on the righthand side of the "
"keyboard between the <keycap>&Windows;</keycap> and &Ctrl; keys. It has a "
"menu icon on it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resizing panels"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have activated two or more views of a spreadsheet, you can move the "
"sizing bar between the views by pressing <keycap>F8</keycap>. A sizing icon "
"appears overtop the sizing bar. Use the arrow keys to move the bar up or "
"down, or left or right. Press <keycap>F8</keycap> again or &Esc; when "
"finished sizing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: a11y.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting focus to widgets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normally, one can use the &Tab; and <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;&Tab;</"
"keycombo> to move focus from one widget to the next in any application. "
"However, in &kcells;, pressing &Tab; does not move the focus; instead it "
"moves the cell selection forwards. You can set focus to any widget that can "
"receive focus by pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F8</"
"keycap></keycombo>. A small lettered box appears overtop each widget on the "
"screen that can receive focus."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: a11y.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press the letter to move focus to the corresponding widget. Press <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F8</keycap></keycombo> again or &Esc; to "
"abandon moving the focus."
msgstr ""
